    "result_text": "The full test suite is green: **272 tests, 0 failures, 0 errors**, BUILD SUCCESS.\n\n## Summary\n\nImplemented digits-only telephone storage with normalization applied before the uniqueness check.\n\n**Changes:**\n\n1. **`src/main/resources/openapi.yml`** \u2014 Relaxed the `telephone` validation pattern from `^[0-9]*$` to `^[0-9 ()-]*$` so formatted input like `(613) 555-0100` passes bean validation instead of being rejected as a 400. (The DTO validation is generated from this spec.)\n\n2. **`OwnerTelephones.java`** (new) \u2014 Small helper with `digitsOnly(String)` that strips every non-digit character (`null`-safe), the single source of the normalization rule.\n\n3. **`BuildOwner.java`** (POST create) \u2014 Normalizes the telephone to digits-only when building the owner, so the **stored** value is digits-only and returned in the `telephone` field.\n\n4. **`ApplyOwner.java`** (PUT update) \u2014 Same normalization on the update path for consistency.\n\n5. **`EnsureOwnerUnique.java`** \u2014 Telephone uniqueness comparison now uses `digitsOnly(...)` for both the candidate and each existing owner, so `(613) 555-0100` and `6135550100` collide. Since `build` runs before `ensureUnique` in the pipeline, normalization is applied before the check either way; this makes it explicit and robust. Updated the class javadoc accordingly.\n\nThe new `Cp11Tests` (both `coreStoresDigitsOnly` and `functionalityNormalisedDuplicateRejected`) pass, along with all existing acceptance, controller, and repository tests.",
